WEBVTT

00:00:29.236 --> 00:00:32.436
It's doing exactly
what it's supposed to do.

00:00:32.476 --> 00:00:34.756
For all its miraculous,

00:00:34.796 --> 00:00:37.956
necessary and pervasive
presence in our lives,

00:00:37.996 --> 00:00:40.356
memory is far from perfect.

00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:44.156
Our brains are not designed
to remember people's names,

00:00:44.196 --> 00:00:45.796
to do something later

00:00:45.836 --> 00:00:48.516
or to catalogue everything we encounter.

00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:52.596
These imperfections are simply
the factory settings.

00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:56.196
Even in the smartest of heads,
memory is fallible.

00:00:56.676 --> 00:01:01.556
A man famous for memorizing
over 100,000 digits of pi